TJR wrote:
>
> Izchak Miller himself coded shopkeepers to be killable. I don't get it
> why people keep making such a fuss about killing the light shopkeeper.

This is the first time I've read an argument in favor of attacking
Izchak the shopkeeper - Izchak Miller coded for that to happen.

> On the other hand, attacking shopkeepers directly is just a very bad
> idea (and useless once you can survive it).

Hmmm.  I've killed mine town priest with missiles because I had not
found any untended altars to convert before Medusa.  Players should be
able to fire missiles through the door at a shopkeeper for the
experience.  With an altar I've carved out the walls to be able to track
the moving priest along the 3 square range.  Shopkeepers repair walls so
that's not an option with a shopkeeper.  If you're marginal on the XP
points for surviving the combat it might be worth the other costs. 
Dubious but possible if you really need a key and have not found one yet
elsewhere.  Definitely an act of desparation.

> With your two bags of
> holding, you could easily have thrown stuff in for the price quote,
> and credit cloned it back out. Selling and re-buying Izchak's
> merchandise in a bag takes a bit longer but is no more difficult than
> at a general store.

Credit cloning and shop robbing is not that difficult.  Using a bag
seems like extra steps, as is throwing the objects.  Walk them in, drop
them, decline to sell them or sell them and rob them back.


